.TH BARDO 1 "October 2026" "bardo 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bardo \- the year as a grid of day files, with a live 3D ASCII field
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bardo
[\fBprint\fR | \fBopen\fR [\fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR|\fBtoday\fR]]
[\fB\-\-txt\fR] [\fB\-\-year\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The first time
.B bardo
runs in a folder it creates a subfolder named for the year, holding one
file per day (365, or 366 in a leap year) and a marker file
.IR .bardo .
Each file starts with a header line naming the day. Anything written
below that line counts as the day's writing.
.PP
With no command,
.B bardo
opens an interactive browser. The grid view shows the year as seven
rows (Monday to Sunday) by week columns. The field view renders every
day as a point in a rotating 3D lattice; written days rise in proportion
to how much was written.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B print
Print the grid and the year's statistics, then exit.
.TP
.BR open " [\fIDATE\fR]"
Open one day in the editor named by
.B VISUAL
or
.BR EDITOR .
The default is today.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-txt
On the first run only, create plain-text
.I .txt
files instead of Markdown
.I .md
files.
.TP
.BI \-\-year " N"
Work on another year's folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " PATH"
Keep the year folder in
.I PATH
instead of the current folder.
.SH KEYS
.TP
Grid
Arrows or \fBh j k l\fR move, \fB[\fR and \fB]\fR jump a month,
Enter opens the day, \fBt\fR returns to today, \fBf\fR opens the field,
\fBr\fR rescans the folder, \fBq\fR quits.
.TP
Field
Arrows turn the lattice, \fB+\fR and \fB\-\fR zoom, space pauses the
spin, \fBh j k l\fR move the cursor, Enter opens the day, \fBg\fR returns
to the grid.
.SH GLYPHS
.nf
@  today            .  not yet          o  passed, empty
+  under 50 words   *  under 250 words  #  250 words or more
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR VISUAL ", " EDITOR
The editor used to open a day. Falls back to nano, then vi.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, print mode uses no color.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./YEAR/YYYY-MM-DD.md
One file per day.
.TP
.I ./YEAR/.bardo
Marks the folder as initialized and records the file format.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Python, Bash and BASIC editions in the same repository read and
write the same folder.
